{"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"topicSections":[{"title":"Putting events in sessions","anchor":"Putting-events-in-sessions","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/Events\/Enricher\/sessions(kinds:file:fileID:function:line:column:)","doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/Events\/Enricher\/sessions(timeout:kinds:file:fileID:function:line:column:)","doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionEventKind","doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/NonPositiveSessionTimeout"]},{"title":"Reading a record’s session","anchor":"Reading-a-records-session","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionKey"]},{"title":"Session events","anchor":"Session-events","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionStarted","doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionEnded"]},{"title":"Sampling whole sessions","anchor":"Sampling-whole-sessions","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/Trackers\/Sampler\/sessions(where:rate:)"]}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Put every event a tracker tracks in a session, and sample whole sessions.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/sessions"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sessions are opt-in. Add the sessions enricher to the ones a tracker is built with, and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tracker’s worker sets each record’s "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionKey"},{"type":"text","text":" to its session’s identifier. A session goes on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"while each event comes less than the timeout (30 minutes by default) after the one before it,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"measured between the records’ timestamps. The first event after a longer gap starts a new session."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The enricher tracks "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionStarted","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" before each session’s first event, and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionEnded","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before that from the second session on, carrying the ended session’s duration. A run’s last session"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has no "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionEnded","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": a session ends only when an event comes after the timeout. Pass "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kinds:"},{"type":"text","text":" to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"track only one kind of session event, or neither; every record still carries its key."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A session’s identifier is a version 7 UUID: the session’s start in Unix milliseconds, then random","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bits. It is held in the enricher’s memory only, never written to disk, and a new tracker, as on the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"next launch, starts a new session. Records a store kept from an earlier run carry no key.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Sampler.sessions(rate:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" keeps or drops every record of a session alike, its session events with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it, by the record’s ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionKey","type":"reference"},{"text":". It needs the sessions enricher among the tracker’s enrichers.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For the app, device, operating system, locale and network an event was tracked on, use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StandardContext"},{"type":"text","text":". For the app’s opens and moves to the background, use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LifecycleTracking"},{"type":"text","text":":"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ApplicationOpened"},{"type":"text","text":" after a long time in the background starts a new session here, though"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"neither module knows about the other."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import Sessions","import Trackers","","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [try .sessions(timeout: .seconds(15 * 60), kinds: [.started])])","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\"))  \/\/ tracks SessionStarted, then SignedUp, both with the same SessionKey"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/sessionsandstandardcontext","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers sessions beside the standard context, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/samplingevents","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers sampling."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Sessions"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","title":"Sessions","externalID":"Sessions","symbolKind":"module"},"references":{"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/samplingevents":{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.gi